}}

==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Shadow & Cat''' at level 10.

==Strategy/Usage==
With arguably one of the most questionable sets of stats and abilities, Shadow is an ultimately difficult to use, but rewarding option against his target traits; his blazing‑fast speed of 95 can occasionally work against his standing range of 520 and his fragility. For his target traits specifically, this can be absolutely terrible: Darks have some of the highest DPS in the game, and burrowing Zombies can completely separate him from the rest of your Cat Army. However, what stops him from becoming a suicidal unit (like [[The Grateful Crane (Uber Rare Cat)|Ultima Galaxy Cosmo]] or [[Momotaro (Uber Rare Cat)|The Peach Devils]]) is his lack of attack delay and 1-second backswing, meaning he won't usually clip immediately after an enemy staggers and loses its hitbox, not to mention Dark and Zombie backliners tend to be few and far between, making him generally safe to use against them. Furthermore, his cost and recharge are reasonable for his performance. While he isn't a great generalist, his [[Massive Damage]] ability bumps up his output significantly, allowing him to repeatedly stagger his target traits with terrifying ease.

[[Immune to Slow|His]] [[Immune to Toxic|immunities]] let him be a decent counter to [[Big Peng Z]] as well as [[Zollow]]/[[Casaurian Darkjo]], and work well in mixed stages featuring [[Gobble]], as he can comfortably engage them at a distance. They also prevent him from getting stunlocked by [[Lophiiformes Angaburu]], meaning he has good matchups in all stages of the game (including endgame against [[Oldstrich]]).

Even with all of this, Shadow is best used in shorter, or more densely packed stages for optimal performance. Given the opportunity, he will abandon the rest of your Cat Army and launch himself towards the enemy base, potentially summoning a boss or getting himself killed outright unless deployed with caution.

